  "family-d5": {
    "photoOrder": [
      "family-img-1520"
    ],
    "leadPhotoId": "family-img-1520",
    "text": "We all slept in (except for Steve obviously) and decided to take it easy while the rain fell. Michelle and David went to see Die Odyssee and Dad and Mom went to a brockie in Luzern (important purchases included a new quick-dry towel & a 1 chifff deck of cards). Mom cooked us all dinner (delicious potatoes!) and we ate outside as the rain let up.",
    "date": "17 Aug",
    "title": "Luzern Rain Day"
  },
  "family-d6": {
    "photoOrder": [
      "family-snapseed-camera-capture-20260818-081450-402",
      "family-img-1525",
      "family-snapseed-camera-capture-20260818-104535-118",
      "family-img-5081",
      "family-snapseed-camera-capture-20260818-105419-043",
      "family-snapseed-camera-capture-20260818-105455-450",
      "family-img-2870",
      "family-snapseed-camera-capture-20260818-110323-609",
      "family-img-2880",
      "family-img-2881",
      "family-snapseed-camera-capture-20260818-111028-981",
      "family-img-2883",
      "family-img-1559",
      "family-img-2886",
      "family-img-2887",
      "family-snapseed-camera-capture-20260818-162911-897",
      "family-snapseed-camera-capture-20260818-162931-975",
      "family-img-5098",
      "family-img-5099",
      "family-img-1584",
      "family-img-1589",
      "family-img-5102"
    ],
    "leadPhotoId": "family-img-2880",
    "text": "We started our day at the Luzern Market before the real journey even began. We took the scenic train along the lakes to Brienz and then hustled to catch the ferry to Interlaken. The water was pristine, including the cigarette butt from the POS in first class.\n\nIn Interlaken, we picnicked at the park, ate some lunch, napped at the park, and walked downtown (in some order). We then caught the train to Lauterbrunnen to see the waterfalls and hang out with all of our closest friends (the other tourists). Michelle and David picked up a 6-pack as well before carrying on (which they would lug around all day).\n\nWe then headed up to Mürren to see the high alps (Jungfraujoch, Eiger, Mönch). By now the exhaustion was already kicking in but there was still a lot of day left at 5pm 🤡. Back into Interlaken we went and got Swiss food for dinner (raclette & rösti 🧀)! We caught the 8pm train back and got back into Luzern by 10pm 💀.",
    "date": "18 Aug",
    "title": "The Marathoner Tag",
    "tagline": "\"This ****ing day\" -Michelle"
  },
